 "lines": [
  [
   "hook",
   "Chile is longer than the distance from Lisbon to Moscow."
  ],
  [
   "thin",
   "But it's so thin, you could drive across it in an afternoon."
  ],
  [
   "ask",
   "So how did a country end up shaped like this?"
  ],
  [
   "wall",
   "First, the wall."
  ],
  [
   "wall",
   "The Andes tower up to nearly seven thousand meters, boxing Spanish Chile against the Pacific."
  ],
  [
   "war",
   "Then, the war."
  ],
  [
   "war",
   "In 1879, Chile fought Bolivia and Peru for the nitrate-rich Atacama Desert, and won."
  ],
  [
   "war2",
   "It took this whole northern strip. Bolivia has had no coast ever since."
  ],
  [
   "deal",
   "Finally, the deal."
  ],
  [
   "deal",
   "In 1881, Chile and Argentina split the south along the highest peaks of the Andes."
  ],
  [
   "deal2",
   "Argentina got the plains of Patagonia. Chile kept the coast."
  ],
  [
   "end",
   "A wall, a war, and a deal. That's the map answer."
  ]
 ],
